y configuration before purchasing.\n\nSeller: ECO-WORTHY\n\n## More websites to explore\n\n- \ue200url\ue202Renogy Tiny Home Solar Kits\ue202https://www.renogy.com/collections/tiny-home-kits\ue201 \u2014 small to medium complete systems.\n- \ue200url\ue202SunGoldPower Cabin & Tiny Home Kits\ue202https://sungoldpower.com/collections/cabine-tiny-home-kits\ue201 \u2014 larger off-grid systems with 120V/240V output.\n- \ue200url\ue202Tiny Home Power Custom Kits\ue202https://www.tinyhomepower.com/customizable-kits.html\ue201 \u2014 customizable systems using Victron equipment.\n\n## What size solar kit do you need?\n\n| Tiny home usage | Suggested solar array | Battery storage |\n|--------|--------|--------|\n| Weekend cabin, basic appliances | 800\u20131,500W | 3\u20135kWh |\n| Full-time tiny home, no electric heating | 2\u20134kW | 10\u201315kWh |\n| Tiny home with air conditioning | 4\u20136kW+ | 15\u201325kWh+ |\n\nThese are starting estimates; actual sizing depends on daily consumption, location, and winter sunlight.\n\n**Are you looking for a solar kit to buy for your own tiny home, or researching websites and products that appear in ChatGPT web search**"}]}     

